m III. the corporation consists of an alderman, who is chosen yearly, 12 capital burgesses, and 4 assistants, landholders and commoners. Here is an almshouse for 4 men and 4 women, and near the bridge an hospital for lepers, where it is supposed there was formerly a nunnery. This town drives a considerable trade in the woollen manufacture;
Malmesbury, has a market on Saturday, and three fairs. It has sent members to parliament ever since the 26th of Edward I.

William of Malmesbury. See William.
